<title>USA: Lojas Arupa to buy back 250 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Lojas Arupa to buy back 250 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lojas Arapua SA said Tuesday that the company has decided to acquire 250 million of its peferred book-entry shares, all without par value.</p>
<p>The company said the shares are to be held in the treasury and will be disposed of in due course, without resulting in a reduction of its share capital, subject to certain conditions, including that the shares be acquired on a stock exchange at market prices, and that the acquisition be made with retained earnings.</p>
<p>Lojas Arapua is a specialty retailer of household appliances and consumer electronics with 258 stores throughout Brazil.</p>
</text>
